<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/08b9690445eb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Israeli Military Using AI to Select Targets in Gaza With 'Rubber Stamp' From Human Operator: Report" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3621" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0b645caf4527> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The officials, quoted in an extensive investigation by the online publication jointly run by Palestinians and Israelis, said that the AI-based tool was called “Lavender” and was known to have a 10% error rate." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7536" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1c7baf00756b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "‘Lavender’: The AI machine directing Israel’s bombing spree in Gaza" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3620" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/202ddec8a74c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "And in an attempt to meet their commanders’ demands, they came to rely on Lavender, which generated a database of individuals believed to have ‘militant’ characteristics." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5946" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/20eb8711ec18> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Lavender AI system reportedly works by analyzing information collected on almost all of the 2.3 million Palestinians in the Gaza Strip “through a system of mass surveillance,” assessing the likelihood of any given person belonging to Hamas in an opaque ranking system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3621" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/29f18a45ab2c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Israel offers a glimpse into the terrifying world of military AI" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3651" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2b1a3525c07e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "White House national security spokesperson John Kirby told CNN on Thursday that the United States was looking into the media reports on the apparent AI tool." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3651" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2dc58298d26b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "the country’s military “almost completely relied” on Lavender during the early weeks of the war, despite the fact that it was known to misidentify potential targets as terrorists." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3621" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3cf0ed06775b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lavender AI program Israel kill lists Gaza Hamas war" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5946" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4a0de57d7a0e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This was used alongside another AI-based decision support system, called the Gospel, which recommended buildings and structures as targets rather than individuals." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3641" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4dd7e9b65f57> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Israel reportedly used ‘Lavender’ AI system to ID thousands of dubious targets in Gaza war" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5948" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/51e88f3954e4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In 2021, a book titled “The Human-Machine Team: How to Create Synergy Between Human and Artificial Intelligence That Will Revolutionize Our World” was released in English under the pen name “Brigadier General Y.S.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7570" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5753a72716a7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Israel also loosened its threshold for the number of civilians it was acceptable to kill as “collateral damage,” a report that’s consistent with previous leaks published in Haaretz about new rules of engagement after October 7." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3621" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/59b2c4efd0f7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "‘The machine did it coldly’: Israel used AI to identify 37,000 Hamas targets" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3641" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/61374490b43b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Additional automated systems, including one called \"Where's Daddy?\" also revealed here for the first time, were used specifically to track the targeted individuals and carry out bombings when they had entered their family's residences." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3620" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6240bd7c0a00> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[7536] The IDF said 'analysts must conduct independent examinations, in which they verify that the identified targets meet the relevant definitions in accordance with international law and additional restrictions stipulated in the IDF directives.'" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7536" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/62b242cb8268> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Israeli military's bombing campaign in Gaza used a previously undisclosed AI-powered database that at one stage identified 37,000 potential targets based on their apparent links to Hamas, according to intelligence sources involved in the war." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3641" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/68c498cde124> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5946] A joint investigation by +972 Magazine and Local Call has revealed that Israel Defense Forces made use of an AI program called Lavender to identify potential Hamas militants in the aftermath of the attacks perpetrated last year." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5946" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/68e0e1083299> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Lavender learns to identify characteristics of known Hamas and [Palestinian Islamic Jihad] operatives, whose information was fed to the machine as training data, and then to locate these same characteristics — also called “features” — among the general population, the sources explained." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3621" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6908f1265038> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "the tool, trained by Israeli military data scientists, sifted through a huge trove of surveillance data and other information to generate targets for assassination." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3651" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/712ee0db76a2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This was used alongside another AI-based decision support system, called the Gospel, which recommended buildings and structures as targets rather than individuals." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5945" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/726d0d42207f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5945] The testimony from the six intelligence officers, all who have been involved in using AI systems to identify Hamas and Palestinian Islamic Jihad (PIJ) targets in the war..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5945" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/768f1a552f05> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Israeli intelligence sources reveal use of 'Lavender' system in Gaza war and claim permission given to kill civilians in pursuit of low-ranking militants." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5945" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/77cf19787de3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "What it meant in the past was that these are particular individuals, who are senior-ranking commanders in Hamas or Islamic Jihad military wings." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3656" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7910e65c0a58> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Their unusually candid testimony provides a rare glimpse into the first-hand experiences of Israeli intelligence officials who have been using machine-learning systems to help identify targets during the six-month war." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3641" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/813935e5b772> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Formally, the Lavender system is designed to mark all suspected operatives in the military wings of Hamas and Palestinian Islamic Jihad (PIJ), including low-ranking ones, as potential bombing targets." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3620" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/827d86d7737f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "President Biden reportedly called on Israel to change course and take demonstrable steps to better preserve civilian life and enable the flow of aid." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3651" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/83b09cb1510d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "So you're willing to take the margin of error of using artificial intelligence, risking collateral damage and civilians dying, and risking attacking by mistake, and to live with it, they added." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3641" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9eaa1f7bfd0d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[7570] Formally, the Lavender system is designed to mark all suspected operatives in the military wings of Hamas and Palestinian Islamic Jihad (PIJ), including low-ranking ones, as potential bombing targets." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7570" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9fb158135bca> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Lavender software analyzes information collected on most of the 2.3 million residents of the Gaza Strip through a system of mass surveillance, then assesses and ranks the likelihood that each particular person is active in the military wing of Hamas or PIJ." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7570" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a119b60f1941> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5946] A joint investigation by +972 Magazine and Local Call has revealed that Israel Defense Forces made use of an AI program called Lavender to identify potential Hamas militants in the aftermath of the attacks perpetrated last year." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5946" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a87d3d3a0692> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The +972 Magazine-Local Call probe further revealed that the Lavender program joined another AI system — The Gospel — which was previously reported about too." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5946" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b0b1dd1232b3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Israel is using artificial intelligence to help pick bombing targets in Gaza, report says" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "7536" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bd9b7982134b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It reportedly used machine learning to identify characteristics of militants and assigned people a score of 1-100, according to military sources, based on factors including association with suspected militants and frequently changing their phone." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5946" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c4ff2fe95c27> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The story revealed how the Israeli military had used the program to identify suspected militants, which in practice meant that tens of thousands of Palestinians had their homes marked as legitimate targets for bombing, with minimal human oversight." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3656" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c6fe64ac67a6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It further argued that Lavender was simply a database whose purpose was to cross-reference intelligence sources, in order to produce up-to-date layers of information on the military operatives of terrorist organisations." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5946" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/da1438c94f2d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to them, Lavender had played a significant role in the war, processing huge troves of data to quickly identify “junior” operatives to target." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5946" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ddfbe00430d0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "1 intelligence officer told The Guardian. “We were told: now we have to f**k up Hamas, no matter what the cost." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5946" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/deb7dc879aa7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Their accounts were shared exclusively with the Guardian in advance of publication." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5945" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e5233895354d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Another automated system used in conjunction with Lavender, dubbed “Where’s Daddy?” has been used to strike targets inside their family homes." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3621" .

